# CloudDesk

CloudDesk is a small full-stack AWS portfolio project built with React,
Express, TypeScript, Docker, EC2, Cognito, DynamoDB, S3, and CloudFront.

## Features

- Cognito sign-in with Authorization Code and PKCE.
- Private tasks stored separately for each user.
- International news loaded by the Express API from RSS feeds.
- Weather and city search loaded directly from Open-Meteo.
- Docker deployment to a small EC2 instance.

## Project structure

```text
frontend-react/       React frontend
backend-express/      Express and TypeScript API
infra-express/        EC2, DynamoDB, ECR, S3, IAM, and CodeBuild
infra/                Cognito CloudFormation template
.github/workflows/    CI and deployment workflows
```

## Express routes

```text
GET    /health
GET    /api/v1/tasks
POST   /api/v1/tasks
PATCH  /api/v1/tasks/:taskId
DELETE /api/v1/tasks/:taskId
GET    /api/v1/news
```

All `/api/v1` routes require a Cognito access token.

## Local development

```bash
cd backend-express
cp .env.example .env
npm install
npm run dev
```

In another terminal:

```bash
cd frontend-react
npm install
npm run dev
```

The production frontend is served from CloudFront. Requests under `/api/v1/*`
are forwarded to the Express container on EC2.
